Be perfect, just as your Father in heaven is perfect.
Giving to people in need.
Be careful not to do "good deeds" before people. Do not do them so that people can see you. If you do them, your Father who is in heaven will not reward you.
In order to give to the needy, do not advertise, do not sound the trumpet. Do not be like those people who pretend to be pious. They advertise what they do in the synagogues and in the streets. They want people to honor them. What I am going to tell you is true. They have received their full reward.
So that you give to the needy, let not your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
Then I gave you so that it would be secret. Your father will reward you. He sees what you do in secret. Prayer.
In order to pray, don't be like the people who pretend to be holy. They like to stand and pray in the synagogues and on street corners. They like for people to see them. What I am about to tell you is true. They have already received their full reward.
In order to pray, go into your room. Close the door and pray to your father who cannot be seen. He will reward you. Your father sees what is done in secret.
In your prayer, do not cease to speak at length like those who have no religion. They think that they will be heard because they speak at length.
Don't be like them. Your father knows what you need before you ask him.
Like that, you must pray. "Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.
Let your kingdom come. Let the will be done on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us today our daily bread.
Forgive our sins, how can we also forgive those who wronged us.
We have not been made to fall into sin when we are deceived. We have been saved from the evil one.
Forgive people when they wrong you. If you do this, your father who is in heaven will also forgive you.
If you do not forgive the people their sins, your father will not forgive you your sins. Fasting.
In order to walk without eating, do not frown your face sadly like people who pretend to be holy. They keep their faces very sad. They want to show people that they are fasting. What I will tell you is true. They took their full reward.
If you go without eating, put olive oil on your head. Wash your face.
Afterwards, the others don't know that you are fasting. Only your father, whom they cannot see, knows. He is the one who will reward you. Your father sees what is done in secret. Hide the treasures in the sky.
Do not hide wealth for yourselves on earth. Corrosion and rust can destroy them. Thieves can break in and steal them.
Sell what you have and give to the poor. Then you will have treasure in heaven. Where a dead body is, there the vultures will gather. The fine display of your celestial tent, O God, like a cloak upon you, the beauty of heaven's display, a glorious sight to see! When the clouds are the clothing of His court, a glory for His highness! He binds the waters in His thick clouds; the clouds are not torn apart by them. He covers the sky in clouds and scatters His light through it. He makes it rain on the earth and sends water on the fields. He sends forth springs into the valleys; they make the seeds grow and the plants sprout. The clouds pour down rain; the mountains hear it and clap their hands together in joy. For you, O God, send light and fire into the sky, and you send rain and dew upon the earth. You make the fields green with grass and clothe the trees with leaves. The mountains stand tall like kings, and the valleys lie low like servants. But when the storm comes, O God, and the lightning flashes, you show your power to everyone. You make the rain fall on the fields and fill the rivers with water. You make the trees grow tall and bear fruit, and you make the grass grow green and cover the fields. And when the sun rises, O God, and its light shines on the earth, you show your goodness to everyone. You make the birds sing in the trees and fill the air with their music. You make the flowers bloom in the fields and fill the air with their fragrance. And when the night comes, O God, and the stars begin to shine in the sky, you show your beauty to everyone. You make the moon rise in the sky and fill the darkness with its light. You make the fireflies flash in the fields and fill the air with their twinkling lights. And when the children see all these wonders, O God, they lift up their voices in joy and praise your holy name for all the goodness and beauty you have created in the world.
Your heart is where your treasure is.
The eye is like a lamp for the body. If your eyes are bright, your whole body will be filled with light.
If your eye is bad, then your whole body will be filled with darkness. If the light within you is darkness, then how great is that darkness!
There is no one who can serve two masters at the same time. They will hate one of them and love the other. Or they will be loyal to one and dislike the other. You cannot serve both God and money at the same time. Don't worry.
Let me tell you, don't worry. Don't worry about your life, what you will eat or drink. And don't worry about your body, what you will wear. Aren't there more important things in life than eating? Aren't there more important things for the body than clothing?
Look, there are birds in the sky. They do not sow or gather grain. They do not store grain in barns. But your Father in heaven feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?
Can you add even one hour to your life by worrying?
Why worry about clothes? Look how the wild flowers grow. They don't work and make clothes.
Hani, let me tell you. Even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of those lilies.
If thus God clothes the wild grass, He will not clothe you, is it better? This grass exists only today. Tomorrow it will be thrown into the fire. Your faith is very small!
Don't worry. Don't say, "What are we going to eat?" or, "What are we going to drink?" or, "What are we going to wear?"
People without self-restraint run after all these things. Your Father in heaven knows what you need.
Seek first the Kingdom of God and His righteousness. Do whatever He tells you to do. Then all these things will be given to you as well.
Don't worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow will worry about itself. Every day has its own problems.
Be fair when you judge others.
Do not judge others, and then no one will judge you.
You will be judged by the same standards you judge others. You will be measured by the same yardstick you use to measure others.
You see a speck of sawdust in your friend's eye. But you don't notice the wooden beam in your own eye.
How can you possibly say to your friend, "Let me get some of this dirt out of your eye"? How can you possibly say that with a sliver of wood in your own eye?
Hey there, demonstrator! First, remove the beam from your own eye. Then you can see clearly to remove the splinter from your friend's eye.
Do not give what is sacred to the dogs. Do not throw your pearls before the swine. If you do that, they may trample them under their feet. Then they may turn back and tear you to pieces. Ask, seek, knock
Ask, and it will be given to you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and the door will be opened to you.
He who asks shall find. He who seeks shall find. The door shall be opened to him who knocks.
Which of you would give him a stone?
And we do not assume that he asks for a fish. Which of you will give him a snake?
Even if you are evil, you know how to give good gifts to your children. How much more, then, will your Father in heaven give good gifts to those who ask him!
In everything, treat others as you would like to be treated. This is what is written in the Torah and the Prophets. The great and small gates.
I will enter my Lord's kingdom through the narrow gate. The gate is wide and the road is broad that leads to death and hell. Many people go along this road.
The door is small and the path is narrow, which leads to life. Few are those who find it. A tree and its fruit.
Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.
You can know who they really are by what they do. "Do people pick grapes from bushes or pick figs from thistles?
How how, every good tree gives good fruits. But the bad tree gives bad fruits.
A good tree does not produce bad fruit. And a bad tree does not produce good fruit.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down. It is thrown into the fire.
You can know every tree by its fruit.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only those who do the will of my Father in heaven.
Many will say to me on that day, 'Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in your name and drive out demons in your name? Did we not perform many miracles in your name?'
Then I will tell them plainly, 'I never knew you. Away from me, you evildoers!' The wise builder and the foolish builder.
So, everyone who hears my words and puts them into practice is like a wise man. He builds his house on the rock.
Rain is falling. Water is rising. Wind is blowing and hitting that house. But it won't fall. It's built on rock.
But everyone who hears my words and does not put them into practice is like a foolish man. He builds his house on sand.
The rain is falling. The water is rising. The wind is blowing and hitting that house. And it falls with a loud sound.
Jesus continued to say all these things. The crowds were amazed at his teaching.
He taught like one who had authority. He did not speak like their teachers of the law.
Jesus Heals a Man Who Had a Skin Disease
Jesus came down from the mountain. Great crowds followed him.
A man who had a skin disease came and got down on his knees in front of Jesus. He said, "Lord, if you are willing to make me 'clean,' you can do it."
Jesus stretched out his hand and touched the man. "I am willing," he said, "to make him clean." Immediately the leprosy left him and he was clean.
Then Jesus said to him, "Do not tell this to anyone. Go and show yourself to the priest. Offer the gift that Moses commanded. So it will be a testimony to them." A Roman centurion who believed.
When Jesus entered Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him and asked him to help him.
"Lord," he said, "my servant lies at home and can't move. He is suffering terribly."
Jesus said, "I must go and heal him."
The commander replied, "Lord, I am not good enough to have you come into my house. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.
I myself am a man under authority. And I have soldiers who obey my commands. We say to this one, 'Go,' and he goes. We say to that one, 'Come,' and he comes. We say to my servants, 'Do this,' and they do it."
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed. He said to his disciples, "Truly I tell you, I have not found anyone in Israel with such great faith."
I tell you, many are coming from the east and west. They will take their places at the feast in the kingdom of heaven. They will be reclining at the table with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.
But as for those who think that they belong to the kingdom, they will be thrown out into the darkness. There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.
Then Jesus said to the Roman leader, "Go! Just as you believed, so will it be done." And his servant was healed at that very hour. Jesus heals many people.
When Jesus came into Peter's house, he saw Peter's mother-in-law. She was lying in bed. She had a fever.
Jesus touched her hand, and the fever left her. She got up and began to serve him.
When evening came, they brought to Him many who were possessed by demons. He cast out the spirits with a word. He healed all the sick.
He did this to fulfill what the prophet Isaiah had said. He said, "He suffered the things that we should have suffered. He carried in His spirit the diseases that should have been on us." (Isaiah 53:4) Following Jesus has a price.
Jesus saw the crowd around him. He gave his disciples orders to go to the other side of the Sea of Galilee.
Then the teacher of the law came to him and said, "Rabbi, I will follow you wherever you go."
Jesus answered, "Foxes have dens and birds of the sky have nests. But the Son of Man has no place to lay his head."
Another follower said to him, "Lord, first let me go and bury my father."
But Jesus said to him, "Follow Me. Let the dead bury their dead." Jesus Calms the Storm.
Jesus got into a boat. His disciples followed him.
Suddenly, a severe storm struck the lake. The waves battered the boat. As for Issa, he was sleeping.
